# Film grain engine — overview

A web app that applies **organic film grain** to still photos. Python/PyTorch
image service behind a React UI, shipped as a **single FastAPI service** that
serves the built client. Deep reference lives in `CLAUDE.md` and `TOPIC.md`.

## In scope (the point of the app)

Detail destruction, edge softening/noising, grain, halation, chromatic edge
fringing. These are what the pipeline exists to do.

## Deferred — do NOT tune without asking

Colour grading in general: tone curves, contrast, toe/shoulder, split toning,
highlight desaturation, base fog, `vibrance`, `brightness`. The engine
implements them and exposes sliders, but they **ship neutral (0)** so the
pipeline is a colour pass-through. Do not fold them into presets or tune them.

## Quality beats speed — an explicit user decision

Latency is accepted. Do **not** clamp octaves, lattice density, blur radii,
supersampling or preview resolution for performance alone. If a quality/speed
trade-off appears, take quality and expose speed as opt-in.

## Layout

```
server/params.py   parameter schema -- SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for engine + UI
server/engine.py   the pipeline (module docstring states the invariants)
server/imageio.py  decode/encode, incl. a hand-written 16-bit RGB PNG encoder
server/main.py     FastAPI service
web/src/App.tsx    UI; slider panel generated from GET /api/params
web/src/api.ts     typed client
tests/verify.py    engine invariant checks -- run after touching engine.py
presets/           preset library -- .json files, not code
run.sh / dev.sh    production-from-source / hot-reload dev
build.sh           compiles a distribution into build/
```

`TOPIC.md` was originally Gemini-generated and is **not authoritative**; it has
been rewritten to match what was actually built.
